# Line endings.
#
# Every text blob committed to this repo is already LF. Without this file, a Windows checkout
# with core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF working copies, and Prettier (which defaults to
# endOfLine: "lf") then reports those files as style violations even though they are
# byte-identical to HEAD. That is exactly what happened on 2026-09-20: `pnpm run format:check`
# failed on 22 files locally while CI, which checks out on Linux, passed on the same commit.
#
# Pinning eol=lf makes every checkout match what is committed, on every platform, so the
# working tree and `format:check` can no longer disagree for line-ending reasons alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The gzip feed fixtures carry CR bytes inside their binary payload. `text=auto` already
# detects them as binary, but these are decompressed by tests where corruption would be
# silent, so state it explicitly rather than relying on the heuristic.
*.gz binary
